From 05e50e392aef1901a1a5eeb7f3e51e42dc378172 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 21:09:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07576/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-5828: tool-calling
 orientation + multi-step lookahead

Operator directive following GAP-ARC-REACTIVE-FILTER-MYOPIC: add real
multi-step lookahead, and allow up to 12 tool-calling/REPL turns per
decision, inspect history, reason, then commit one action.

Reuses arc_solver_kit.OfflineSolver's best-first search with
replay-from-reset backtracking (already built, tested across 25 games)
rather than a new search algorithm -- this module only supplies its
three pluggable hooks, backed by a bounded tool-calling loop over a
small safe dispatch table (inspect_frame/inspect_cell/count_color/
inspect_history/list_available_actions), a disclosed scope reduction
from Duck Harness's full sandboxed REPL for a 9B model already shown
to struggle with unconstrained structured output. The final commit
turn requests a RANKED SET of candidates (not one action) so the
reused search engine has real branching to backtrack into, not a
straight-line greedy rollout.

Two real bugs found via smoke test, not assumed: the model initially
looped on the exact same tool query 5 times without ever committing
(fixed via dedup + an urgency nudge as the turn budget runs low); and
OfflineSolver's own internal warmup-replay bookkeeping polluted the
model-facing history and confidence tracking -- the obvious fix
(comparing action VALUES) was itself wrong, since a genuine model
choice matching the warmup action got silently swallowed too, fixed
with a sentinel label that can never collide with a real JSON-encoded
candidate.

22 unit tests (scripted proposer, no GPU). Real empirical A/B on the
same 3 games as both prior mechanisms is running separately; results
land in a follow-up commit regardless of outcome.

